    {"id": "REQ-TC-08", "ssot": "§23 TC-08", "requirement": "Conformance test TC-08 (SSOT §23).", "kind": "tested", "status": "pass", "conformance_test": "TC-08", "equations": ["EQ-IGN-2", "EQ-HAZARD-1", "EQ-OBS-2", "EQ-PREC-SM-1", "EQ-ALLO-1", "EQ-COST-1", "EQ-VAL-1", "EQ-NE-1"], "claims": ["CL-43", "CL-44", "CL-45", "CL-46"], "lean": ["Apgi.hazardLik_shift", "Apgi.hazardLik_rescale", "Apgi.hazardLik_not_injective", "Apgi.traj_gain_product", "Apgi.gain_product_not_injective", "Apgi.traj_scaleAllo", "Apgi.scaleAllo_not_injective", "Apgi.traj_weights_eta_zero"], "tests": ["test_recovery.py::test_recovery_gate_theta", "test_recovery.py::test_recovery_gate_gamma", "test_recovery.py::test_recovery_fails_without_the_scale_anchor", "test_recovery.py::test_tc08a_common_offset_twin", "test_recovery.py::test_tc08b_gain_product_twin", "test_recovery.py::test_tc08c_joint_scale_twin", "test_recovery_pipeline.py::test_simulator_matches_core_step", "test_recovery_pipeline.py::test_tc08g_scale_twin", "test_recovery_pipeline.py::test_report_is_current", "test_recovery_pipeline.py::test_sbc_calibrated", "test_recovery_pipeline.py::test_gate_outcomes", "test_recovery_pipeline.py::test_tc08e_tradeoff_present", "test_recovery_pipeline.py::test_tc08g_cost_weight_unidentified", "test_recovery_pipeline.py::test_tc08g_second_weights_are_what_the_study_fits", "test_recovery_pipeline.py::test_tc08g_second_weights_trade_off", "test_recovery_pipeline.py::test_tc08f_free_scale_costs_little_here", "test_recovery_pipeline.py::test_out_of_sample_prediction", "test_recovery_pipeline.py::test_sbc_detects_a_mismatched_likelihood", "test_recovery_pipeline.py::test_failed_recovery_dispositions"], "limitation": "TC-08a–c and the exact part of TC-08g (η_θ enters only through η_θ·c and η_θ·v) are proved in Apgi/Identifiability.lean and twinned. The §17 gate passes for θ_eff and γ_sig of the observation model (r 0.985 / 0.953, error 0.039 / 0.061; N = 60). The full-pipeline study (task 62b; verification/reports/recovery-pipeline.json; every-step event observation, an upper bound on behavior by CL-46; synthetic design in fixtures/recovery_design.json; 30 subjects per block) runs all four §17 diagnostics: posterior correlations, profile likelihood, SBC (every p > 0.25; shown to detect a mismatched likelihood) and out-of-sample prediction (the posterior predictive beats the block's null in every block). Gate: k_V = η_θ·v₁ passes (r 0.904 fast design / 0.917 block design); γ_NE and g_NE pass (r 0.976 / 0.907; TC-08d posterior correlation +0.20); γ_sig passes with the precision scale free (r 0.985; TC-08f correlation +0.18; the scale is identified only because θ₀ is fixed). τ_θ fails (r 0.753 / 0.480; TC-08e posterior correlation with k_V −0.79 in both designs) and k_C = η_θ·c₁ fails (r 0.30 / 0.36, flat profile likelihood). Round 74 adds the second weights: with τ_θ free and δ_reset known, k_C2 = η_θ·c₂ fails narrowly (r 0.803, error 0.157) and k_V2 = η_θ·v₂ fails (r 0.580), posterior correlation k_C2~k_V2 +0.69 (the events constrain mainly their net effect on θ); with k_C2 and δ_reset both free (block c2_reset) neither passes (r 0.570 / 0.793), correlation −0.59: c₂·B(t−1) and δ_reset·B(t) are the same per-event increment one step apart. §17 dispositions (task 71a, author, 2026-11-27): τ_θ, η_θ·c₁, η_θ·c₂, η_θ·v₂ and the c₂ / δ_reset pair are redesignated as requiring auxiliary measurement (parameters.json recovery_dispositions; test_failed_recovery_dispositions checks that every failing quantity has exactly one); η_θ is reported only through its products (CL-45). Remaining limitations: behavior-level fits are not done (CL-46 bounds them by the event-level study); the 20% gate and the dispositions are proposed readings pending the OSF amendment (B-14).", "record_status": "Proposed", "owner": "Uxod", "approval_date": null},
